The third-party/ directory contains the exact Cargo.lock, a versioned resolved
Linux dependency inventory, full crate license/notice texts, ONNX Runtime 1.24.2
license and third-party notices, and the Rust runtime copyright/license texts.
The inventory conservatively includes build and development dependencies;
it does not assert that every listed package is linked into each executable.
Nested notices from vendored native code are preserved alongside crate notices.

MPL-2.0-covered source for option-ext and ONNX Runtime's pinned Eigen revision is
supplied in third-party/sources. Eigen's build metadata and patches are included
under third-party/onnxruntime-1.24.2. See third-party/README.md for details.
The local LanceDB manifest-only patch is documented in third-party/LANCEDB-PATCHES.md;
its runtime source is unchanged. Its Apache-2.0 license is also in LANCEDB-LICENSE.

ONNX Runtime is statically linked. CUDA bundles additionally carry its CUDA and
shared provider libraries. NVIDIA driver, CUDA runtime, cuRAND and cuDNN libraries
are external dependencies and are NOT redistributed. Neither are the system
libheif, libjpeg-turbo, glibc, libstdc++, Qt/Quickshell or FFmpeg libraries/tools.
Their installation and licensing are provided by the user's operating system.
No implication of endorsement by these projects or their contributors is made.

Model weights/tokenizers are not bundled. First-run setup downloads pinned,
verified assets from onnx-community/embeddinggemma-2-ONNX at the revision recorded
in model-manifest.json. Model/export terms apply separately from this application:
https://huggingface.co/onnx-community/embeddinggemma-2-ONNX
https://huggingface.co/google/embeddinggemma-2
Do not redistribute model assets under the application's MIT license.

SHA256SUMS verifies bundle integrity; it is not a publisher signature.
